# Frontend Conventions

## Component Design & Architecture

- Create small, focused, reusable components with single responsibility
- Prefer functional components over class components
- Use custom hooks for shared stateful logic
- Implement proper prop validation and default values

## State Management

- Keep state as close to where it's used as possible
- Use immutable state updates to prevent side effects
- Avoid prop drilling - use context or state management libraries when needed
- Normalize complex state structures
- Use derived state instead of storing computed values
- Implement proper state cleanup in useEffect hooks

## Performance Optimization

- Implement proper memoization for expensive calculations
- Use lazy loading for components and routes
- Optimize images and media assets
- Implement virtual scrolling for large lists
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders with proper dependency arrays
- Use debouncing and throttling for user input handlers
- Minimize bundle size with code splitting

## User Experience (UX)

- Implement proper loading states for async operations
- Provide meaningful error messages and fallback UI
- Ensure keyboard navigation accessibility
- Use consistent spacing, typography, and color schemes
- Implement proper focus management
- Provide visual feedback for user interactions
- Design for mobile-first responsive layouts

## Accessibility (A11y)

- Use semantic HTML elements appropriately
- Provide proper ARIA labels and descriptions
- Ensure sufficient color contrast ratios
- Implement keyboard navigation support
- Use proper heading hierarchy (h1, h2, h3, etc.)
- Provide alternative text for images
- Test with screen readers and assistive technologies

## Form Handling

- Implement proper form validation on both client and server
- Provide real-time validation feedback
- Use controlled components for form inputs
- Implement proper error handling and display
- Provide clear success and error states
- Use proper input types and attributes
- Implement proper form submission handling

## Event Handling

- Use event delegation for dynamic content
- Implement proper event cleanup to prevent memory leaks
- Use synthetic events when available
- Implement proper event propagation control
- Use debouncing for search and input events
- Handle edge cases in user interactions

## Styling & CSS

- Use CSS custom properties (variables) for consistent theming
- Implement responsive design with mobile-first approach
- Use CSS Grid and Flexbox for layouts
- Avoid inline styles except for dynamic values
- Implement proper CSS organization and structure

## Data Fetching & API Integration

- Implement proper loading and error states
- Use proper caching strategies
- Handle network failures gracefully
- Implement retry logic for failed requests
- Use proper data transformation and normalization
- Implement optimistic updates when appropriate
- Handle race conditions in async operations

## Security Best Practices

- Sanitize user input before rendering
- Implement proper CSRF protection
- Use HTTPS for all communications
- Implement proper content security policies
- Avoid storing sensitive data in client-side storage
- Use proper authentication and authorization checks
- Implement proper XSS protection

## Browser Compatibility

- Test across different browsers and versions
- Use feature detection instead of browser detection
- Implement proper polyfills when needed
- Use progressive enhancement principles
- Handle browser-specific quirks appropriately
- Test on different devices and screen sizes
